hadiths[67]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Treat your sick with charity."
"3359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tanning of leather is itself its purification."
"3360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tanning of the skins of dead (animals) is itself their purification."
"3361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tanning of every hide is itself its purification."
"3362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dihyah al-Kalbi resembled Jibril, Urwah bin Mas'ud al-Thaqafi resembled Isa bin Maryam, and Abd al-Uzza resembled the Dajjal."
"3363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise last night and looked in it, and there was Ja'far flying with the angels, and Hamzah was reclining on a couch."
"3364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold there. I asked: 'Whose palace is this?' It was said: 'It belongs to a young man of Quraysh.' I thought that perhaps it was me, so I asked: 'Who is he?' It was said: 'Umar bin al-Khattab.' (Then he said: O Umar!) Had I not known of your sense of honour, I would have entered it."
"3365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and saw a river there whose two banks were made of tents of pearls. I stretched my hand towards the water flowing in it, and it was fragrant musk. I asked: 'O Jibril, what is this?' He said: 'This is al-Kawthar which Allah has granted you.'"
"3366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and a young girl came to receive me. I asked: 'Whom are you for?' She said: 'For Zayd bin Harithah.'"
"3367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and saw two ranks for Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl."
"3368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and heard the sound of footsteps ahead of me. I asked: 'What are these footsteps?' It was said: 'This is al-Ghumaysa bint Milhan.'"
"3369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and heard the sound of footsteps ahead of me. I asked: 'What are these footsteps?' It was said: 'This is Bilal, walking ahead of you.'"
"3370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and heard a sound of footsteps. I asked: 'What is this?' It was said: 'This is Bilal.' Then I entered Paradise and heard a sound of footsteps. I asked: 'What is this?' It was said: 'This is al-Ghumaysa bint Milhan.'"
"3371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entered Paradise and heard the sound of recitation in it. I asked: 'Who is this?' It was said: 'Harithah bin al-Nu'man.' (Then he said:) That is what righteousness (kindness to parents) is like, that is what righteousness is like!"
"3372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I entered Paradise and heard a sound from one side of it. I asked: 'O Jibril, what is this?' He said: 'This is Bilal, the caller to prayer.'"
"3373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"3374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman entered Hell because of a cat which she had tied up; she neither fed it nor let it go free to eat the insects of the earth, until it (the cat) died."
"3375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A single dirham of usury (riba) which a man consumes knowingly is more grievous (a sin) in the sight of Allah than committing adultery thirty-six times."
"3376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When milking, leave enough milk in the udder to cause more milk to come down."
"3377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt."
"3378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for truthfulness is tranquillity and lying is doubt and suspicion."
"3379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A brother's supplication for his (absent) brother, made behind his back, is not rejected."
"3380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim man's supplication for his (absent) brother, made behind his back, is answered. At his head there is an angel appointed; whenever he supplicates for good for his brother, the angel says: 'Amin, and for you the same.'"
"3381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's supplication for his (absent) brother, made behind his back, is answered, and there is an angel at his head who says: 'Amin, and for you the same.'"
"3382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of the oppressed is answered, even if he is a sinner; the consequence of his sinfulness falls upon himself."
"3383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of Dhu al-Nun (Yunus, peace be upon him), which he made when he was in the belly of the fish: There is no true god except You; glory be to You; indeed, I was among the wrongdoers. Any Muslim man who makes this supplication concerning any matter, Allah will surely answer him."
"3384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave the Abyssinians alone as long as they leave you alone, and leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone."
"3385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave people alone so that they may benefit from one another; but when one of you is asked for advice by his brother, let him advise him."
"3386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave my Companions to me. By the One in whose hand is my soul! Even if you were to spend (in the path of Allah) gold equal to Mount Uhud, you would not reach their deeds."
"3387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave him, for the one who has a right is entitled to speak."
"3388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplications of the distressed are: O Allah, it is Your mercy that I hope for, so do not leave me to myself even for the blink of an eye, and set right all my affairs for me; there is no true god except You."
"3389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He was buried in the soil from which he was created."
"3390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who guides to good is like the one who does it."
"3391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of a whitish (sheep) is more beloved to Allah than that of two black (sheep)."
"3392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of a whitish (sheep) is purer in the sight of Allah than the blood of two black (sheep)."
"3393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Here you are, take your due."
"3394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood money for the fingers and toes is equal: ten camels for each finger."
"3395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood money of a mu'ahad (a non-Muslim living under a covenant) is half the blood money of a free person."
"3396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood money of a mukatab (a slave who has made a contract to buy his freedom) is this: for the portion of him that has been freed, the blood money of a free person in proportion to it, and for the portion that remains in slavery, the blood money of a slave in proportion to it."
"3397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood money of a disbeliever is half the blood money of a believer."
"3398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A dinar that you spend in the path of Allah, a dinar that you spend on freeing a slave, a dinar that you give in charity to a poor person, and a dinar that you spend on your family: the greatest of them in reward is the one you spend on your family."
"3399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who guides to good is like the one who does it."
"3400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal is blind in the left eye and has thick hair. With him will be a Paradise and a Hell; his Hell will (in reality) be Paradise, and his Paradise will (in reality) be Hell."
"3401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal's eye is green."
"3402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal's eye is wiped out (effaced). Between his eyes is written 'Kafir' (disbeliever), which every Muslim will read."
"3403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will have no children, and he will not be able to enter Madinah or Makkah."
"3404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan. He will be followed by peoples whose faces are like layered (hammered) shields."
"3405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplication made between the adhan and the iqamah is answered, so make supplication."
"3406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplication is answered between the adhan and the iqamah."
"3407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplication is worship itself."
"3408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."
"3409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplication benefits against the affliction that has already descended and against that which has not yet descended. So, O servants of Allah, hold fast to supplication."
"3410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This world is sweet and green (attractive). Whoever takes it by its right will be blessed in it. And many a person who plunges into whatever his desires crave will have nothing on the Day of Resurrection except the Fire."
"3411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This world is green and sweet."
"3412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This world is a prison for the believer and a paradise for the disbeliever."
"3413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The whole of this world is provision (something to be enjoyed), and the best provision of this world is a righteous woman."
"3414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This world is cursed, and whatever is in it is cursed, except the remembrance of Allah and what is connected to it, and except a scholar or a student."
"3415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Medicine is also part of the divine decree, and it benefits by the permission of Allah Almighty."
"3416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Medicine is also part of the divine decree, and it benefits whomever Allah wills with whatever He wills."
"3417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The religion is sincere goodwill (nasihah)."
"3418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Debt is of two kinds: whoever dies intending to repay it, I am his guardian (guarantor); and whoever dies not intending to repay it, that is the one from whose good deeds it will be taken (on the Day of Resurrection), for on that day there will be neither dinar nor dirham."
"3419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Debt comes before the bequest, and there is no bequest for an heir."
"3420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The religion is easy, and whoever makes the religion hard for himself, the religion will overpower him."
"3421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A dinar for a dinar, a dirham for a dirham, a sa' of wheat for a sa' of wheat, a sa' of barley for a sa' of barley, and a sa' of salt for a sa' of salt; there is to be no excess in any of these."
"3422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A dinar for a dinar, with no excess between them, and a dirham for a dirham, with no excess between them either."
"3423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A dinar for a dinar, with no excess between them, and a dirham for a dirham, with no excess between them either. So whoever needs silver, let him exchange gold for it, and whoever needs gold, let him exchange silver for it, and the exchange must be hand to hand (on the spot)."
"3424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A dinar is a hoarded treasure, a dirham is a hoarded treasure, and a qirat is a hoarded treasure."
